    "title": "Man dies on highway after being hit by a truck in Fresno - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Christian Valdez No media credit provided. ,\n3 hours ago\nFRESNO, Calif ( KSEE/KGPE ) – A man was killed after being hit by a Dodge pickup on Highway 41 and Divisadero in Fresno, according to the California Highway Patrol.\nOfficers responded to a pedestrian who had been involved in a collision on the freeway around 5:00 p.m. CHP believes that the individual ran east from the center median onto the highway when he was struck by a vehicle traveling north.\nThe pedestrian was pronounced dead at the scene, according to the CHP.\nThe driver is cooperating with investigators, according to the CHP.\n“Signs on the freeway say pedestrians are prohibited for a reason; it is very unsafe,” said Sergeant Bianchi of the California Highway Patrol.\nThe name of the victim has not been officially released.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to CBS47 and KSEE24 | News from YourCentralValley.com.",
    "summary": ", FRESNO, Calif ( KSEE/KGPE ) – A man was killed after being hit by a Dodge pickup on Highway 41 and Divisadero in Fresno, according to the California Highway Patrol. Officers responded to a pedestrian who had been involved in a collision on the freeway around 5:00 p.m. CHP believes that the individual ran east from the center median onto the highway when he was struck by a vehicle traveling north. “Signs on the freeway say pedestrians are prohibited for a reason; it is very unsafe,” said Sergeant Bianchi of the California Highway Patrol.",
